      "title": "Determining Whether a Function Is Continuous at a Given Point"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Select the function that is continuous at $x=1.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The correct answer is shown below.  Indeed, despite the fact that the function has a discontinuity at $x=5$, the graph can be drawn in a neighborhood of $x=1$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/5b08dcf69b65b03cb27d6cce7f08f85eb007503de9085356bc7e4363e157087d.png)\n\n   \n\nAll the other given graphs contain breaks at $x=1$ and it would be impossible to draw them in a neighborhood of $x=1$ without taking the pencil off of the paper.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
