    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Select the function that is continuous at $x=1.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, the only one where we can draw the graph of the function without taking our pencil off of the paper in a neighborhood of $x=1$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/e3f2b2994c054ef3c5356996331b4dc9dde8427c69e5dd101ece20cae2d8c554.png)\n\nAll other given options have breaks or asymptotes at $x=1$, so it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=1$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.",
