      ":question/worked-solution": "The correct answer is shown below.  Indeed, despite the fact that the function has a discontinuity at $x=1$, the graph can be drawn in a neighborhood of $x=-1$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/c923b37b7240318b6f40e89f201164c2653c027fc8c2dd57bad535363ec60b4e.png)\n\n   \n\nAll the other given graphs contain breaks at $x=-1$ and it would be impossible to draw them in a neighborhood of $x=-1$ without taking the pencil off of the paper.",
